course: dictionary
lesson: 15877
title: Uniformly: the same all the way through
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Uniform means all the same. Add -ly and you get uniformly, which tells you how something happens: in the same way everywhere, or for everyone. Look for the clue inside the word.
explain: «The paint was spread uniformly over the wall.» The paint is the same thickness everywhere, with no bare patches and no thick lumps. Try swapping in «evenly» to check: it still makes sense.
explain: In maths and science, uniformly means at the same rate all the time. «The toy car moved uniformly along the track.» It covered the same distance every second, so its speed never changed.
fact: Uniformly means in the same way everywhere, or for everyone.
fact: «Uniformly» comes from «uniform», which means all the same.
fact: In science and maths, uniformly can mean at the same rate all the time.
fact: «The reviews were uniformly good» means every single review was good.
fact: A good check is to swap in «the same way» or «evenly» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The sand was spread uniformly across the playground.» What does uniformly mean here? | Unevenly, in big heaps | Quickly and loudly | Only in one corner | *Evenly, the same everywhere
exercise: «A ball rolled uniformly down the slope.» In maths, what does uniformly tell us? | *It moved at the same rate all the time | It stopped halfway down | It bounced off the wall | It rolled faster and faster
exercise: Ruby says, «The reviews were uniformly good.» Which sentence means the same? | The reviews arrived late | Some reviews were good and some were bad | *Every review was good | Nobody read the reviews
test: «The heat was spread uniformly through the metal pan.» What does uniformly mean in this sentence? | Cracked in two | Only at the edges | *Evenly, the same all over | Too hot to touch
test: A toy train travels uniformly for one minute. What does this tell us? | It goes backwards | It stops often during the minute | It goes faster at the end | *It covers the same distance every second
exam: Which word means the same as uniformly in «The children were dressed uniformly for the play»? | Messily | Differently | *In the same way | Sadly
